{
  "_meta": {
    "title": "Remove object / text from video (SAM 3.1 + Wan2.2 Fun VACE, masked paste-back)",
    "description": "Core nodes + h3-relay LabsH3PrepareVideo + cj_h3_tools. LoadVideo -> LabsH3PrepareVideo (24 fps, ~0.5 MP on the 32-px grid, first 3 s = 73 frames; 4n+1 so it is also a valid VACE length) -> SAM 3.1 text-prompted video tracking (node 31 = what to remove; comma-separated prompts, optional ':N' max detections each) -> SAM3_TrackToMask -> GrowMask -> CJMaskTemporal (max, temporal dilation: a frame the tracker missed stays masked) -> WanVaceToVideo with the original frames, masked area filled neutral grey (VACE's inpaint convention; ungreyed it just re-renders the object), as control video and the mask as control_masks (1 = regenerate), two-stage Wan2.2 Fun VACE sampling (balanced: hi w/o LoRA 8 steps cfg 3.5 0-4, lo + lightx2v cfg 1; fast: LoRA both, 4 steps cfg 1) -> trim to the real frame count -> CJPasteBackSave: the generated pixels are kept only inside the mask, everything else is the source at source resolution, source audio copied. protect_text is off (we are removing text). The video_remove_text action reuses this graph with a text/caption/watermark SAM prompt, more objects, a denser detect interval and a wider mask. A second CJMaskTemporal (node 38, max, radius 4 = the worst distance between a frame and the frame WanVaceToVideo samples for its latent's mask) feeds control_masks and the paste-back's expanded_mask: VACE keeps one frame's mask per 4-frame latent, so a fast limb greyed in a frame the sample missed was copied as grey (smear); with the wider latent mask every greyed pixel is regenerated."
  },
